    <section id="open-research">
      <h2>Open research and data</h2>

      <p>
        I support open and reproducible research wherever legal,
        ethical, and data-protection requirements allow it. Public
        datasets and supporting materials make research processes
        more transparent and allow other researchers to examine,
        reuse, and extend the work.
      </p>

      <div class="extras-resource">
        <h3>
          <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15024172">
            Spanish environmental-crime judgments dataset
          </a>
        </h3>

        <p class="resource-meta">
          Zenodo · Open research dataset · 2015–2024
        </p>

        <p>
          A structured dataset of Spanish judgments concerning the
          environmental offence established in Article 325 of the
          Spanish Criminal Code. The dataset supports legal and
          criminological analysis of environmental-crime adjudication.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="extras-resource">
        <h3>
          <a href="https://portalcientific.uji.es/datos?personaId=1327563">
            UJI research-data record
          </a>
        </h3>

        <p>
          The institutional research-data portal provides access to
          additional datasets, metadata, associated publications,
          and open research outputs.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="extras-resource">
        <h3>
          <a href="https://doi.org/10.12688/openreseurope.24170.2">
            Legal-ecological coding framework
          </a>
        </h3>

        <p class="resource-meta">
          Open Research Europe · 2026
        </p>

        <p>
          An openly published pilot framework connecting legal variables
          from environmental-crime judgments with ecological indicators
          of harm.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

